     "explanation": "The English word ends in -ty, and -ty converts to -dad. So possibility becomes **posibilidad** (poh-see-bee-lee-DAHD), a feminine noun: **Es una posibilidad** — \"It's a possibility.\" The wrong answers apply the other patterns to an ending that does not take them: -ción is for -tion words, -oso for -ous adjectives, -mento for -ment nouns. Notice also that Spanish writes one s where English writes two — Spanish almost never doubles s.",
