     "explanation": "A Spanish question opens with the inverted **¿** and closes with the ordinary **?** — so **¿Cómo estás?** is the only correct form. Dropping the opening mark is a genuine spelling error, not a casual shortcut, and using **¿** at the end is simply the wrong character. The logic is worth holding on to: because Spanish questions use the same words in the same order as statements, the opening mark is the only advance warning you get that the sentence is a question. Exclamations follow the identical rule: **¡Qué bonito!**",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">THE PUNCTUATION PAIR</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"110\" width=\"800\" height=\"170\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"bold\">THE RULE</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"218\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"26\">Questions: inverted opens, normal closes.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"258\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"26\">Exclamations: the same, both required.</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"325\" width=\"900\" height=\"105\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><circle cx=\"170\" cy=\"377\" r=\"30\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"170\" y=\"390\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"32\" font-weight=\"bold\">1</text><text x=\"240\" y=\"368\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"28\">inverted open  +  normal close</text><text x=\"240\" y=\"405\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"24\">correct: this is the only right form</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"455\" width=\"900\" height=\"105\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"170\" cy=\"507\" r=\"30\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"170\" y=\"520\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-size=\"32\" font-weight=\"bold\">2</text><text x=\"240\" y=\"498\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"28\">no opening mark  +  normal close</text><text x=\"240\" y=\"535\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-size=\"24\">a real spelling error, not a shortcut</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"585\" width=\"900\" height=\"105\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"170\" cy=\"637\" r=\"30\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"170\" y=\"650\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-size=\"32\" font-weight=\"bold\">3</text><text x=\"240\" y=\"628\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"28\">inverted open  +  inverted close</text><text x=\"240\" y=\"665\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-size=\"24\">the closing character is wrong</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"715\" width=\"900\" height=\"105\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"170\" cy=\"767\" r=\"30\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"170\" y=\"780\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-size=\"32\" font-weight=\"bold\">4</text><text x=\"240\" y=\"758\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"28\">nothing open  +  inverted close</text><text x=\"240\" y=\"795\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-size=\"24\">both halves wrong at once</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"860\" width=\"900\" height=\"170\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"910\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"bold\">WHY IT MATTERS HERE</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"960\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"24\">Spanish questions reuse the statement word order,</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"1000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"24\">so the opening mark is your only early warning.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "One correct pattern and three ways to get it wrong, with the reason the rule exists."
     }
