    {
     "type": "quiz",
     "question": "You are filling in a form and need to write 15 March 2026 the Spanish way. Which version is right?",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "el 15 de marzo de 2026",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "el marzo 15 de 2026",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "el quince marzo 2026",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "el 15 de Marzo de 2026",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "**el 15 de marzo de 2026**, read aloud as **el quince de marzo de dos mil veintiséis**.\n\nEach wrong answer breaks one rule. \"El marzo 15\" keeps the English month-first order, which Spanish never uses. \"El quince marzo 2026\" drops both instances of **de** — the day needs *de* before the month, and the month needs *de* before the year. And \"de Marzo\" capitalises the month, an English habit that immediately marks a text as translated; Spanish months and days stay in lower case wherever they sit in the sentence.\n\nOne more thing that trips readers rather than writers: in figures, **15/3/2026** is the fifteenth of March. On a Spanish-language form, the day always comes first.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">FLIPPING THE DATE ORDER</text><rect x=\"300\" y=\"95\" width=\"500\" height=\"90\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"152\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"28\">March 15, 2026</text><rect x=\"290\" y=\"230\" width=\"200\" height=\"80\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(59,130,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"390\" y=\"282\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" font-size=\"26\">March</text><rect x=\"610\" y=\"230\" width=\"200\" height=\"80\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(236,72,153,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"710\" y=\"282\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-size=\"26\">15</text><path d=\"M 390 318 L 706 392\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><path d=\"M 683 375 L 712 394 L 679 397 Z\" fill=\"#ffd700\"/><path d=\"M 710 318 L 394 392\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><path d=\"M 421 375 L 388 394 L 417 397 Z\" fill=\"#ffd700\"/><text x=\"90\" y=\"365\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"22\">the order flips</text><rect x=\"290\" y=\"400\" width=\"200\" height=\"80\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(236,72,153,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"390\" y=\"452\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-size=\"26\">15</text><rect x=\"610\" y=\"400\" width=\"200\" height=\"80\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(59,130,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"710\" y=\"452\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" font-size=\"26\">marzo</text><path d=\"M 550 495 L 550 538\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><path d=\"M 533 518 L 550 542 L 567 518 Z\" fill=\"#ffd700\"/><rect x=\"200\" y=\"550\" width=\"700\" height=\"100\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"613\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"30\" font-weight=\"bold\">el 15 de marzo de 2026</text><rect x=\"70\" y=\"690\" width=\"960\" height=\"310\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"742\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"bold\">FOUR THINGS TO GET RIGHT</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"800\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"23\">1</text><text x=\"185\" y=\"800\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"23\">the day comes before the month</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"845\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"23\">2</text><text x=\"185\" y=\"845\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"23\">de sits before the month and before the year</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"890\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"23\">3</text><text x=\"185\" y=\"890\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"23\">the month stays lower case: marzo, not Marzo</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"935\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"23\">4</text><text x=\"185\" y=\"935\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"23\">the year is one number: dos mil veintiseis</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"982\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-size=\"22\">In figures too: 15/3/2026 is the fifteenth of March.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "English gives month then day; Spanish flips them and binds the pieces with de, keeping the month in lower case."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Your Age and the Price: Where Numbers Actually Live",
     "content": "Two situations use numbers more than everything else combined. Learn the frames and the numbers slot straight in.\n\n**Age. Spanish has years rather than being them.**\n\n**¿Cuántos años tienes?** (KWAHN-tohs AH-nyohs TYEH-nehs) — literally \"how many years do you have?\", naturally \"how old are you?\"\n**Tengo veintiocho años.** (TEHN-goh bayn-TYOH-choh AH-nyohs) — literally \"I have twenty-eight years\", naturally \"I'm twenty-eight.\"\n\nThis is the **tener** pattern from lesson 6 doing exactly what it did with hunger and thirst. English *is* an age; Spanish *has* one. Saying **soy veintiocho** is a mistake a Spanish speaker will notice immediately, because it sounds like you are claiming to *be* the number.\n\nFor someone you address formally, the verb shifts: **¿Cuántos años tiene usted?** And **años** must keep its tilde — the same word without it is anatomical, and you did not mean that.\n\n**Price. Three questions, three jobs.**\n\n• **¿Cuánto cuesta?** (KWAHN-toh KWEHS-tah) — how much does it cost? One item.\n• **¿Cuánto cuestan?** — how much do they cost? Several items.\n• **¿Cuánto es?** (KWAHN-toh EHS) — how much is it? The total, at the till.\n\nIn Spain you will hear **¿Cuánto vale?** just as often as *¿Cuánto cuesta?* — same meaning, pick either.\n\nThe answers come back in matching shapes:\n• **Cuesta doce euros.** — It costs twelve euros.\n• **Cuestan treinta euros.** — They cost thirty euros.\n• **Son quince euros con cincuenta.** — That's fifteen euros fifty.\n\nNote **con** where English uses nothing: **doce euros con cincuenta** for 12,50. And note the comma — Spanish writes **12,50** where English writes 12.50, and uses the point for thousands: **1.500 euros**. It is the exact reverse of the English convention, and it is worth a second glance before you agree to a price.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">AGE AND PRICE</text><rect x=\"70\" y=\"105\" width=\"470\" height=\"480\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text x=\"305\" y=\"160\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"bold\">AGE USES TENER</text><text x=\"305\" y=\"218\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"23\">Cuantos anos tienes?</text><text x=\"305\" y=\"255\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"21\">how many years do you have?</text><line x1=\"120\" y1=\"285\" x2=\"490\" y2=\"285\" stroke=\"#888\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"305\" y=\"333\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"24\">Tengo veintiocho anos.</text><text x=\"305\" y=\"370\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"21\">I have twenty-eight years</text><line x1=\"120\" y1=\"400\" x2=\"490\" y2=\"400\" stroke=\"#888\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"305\" y=\"448\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-size=\"24\">Soy veintiocho.</text><text x=\"305\" y=\"485\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-size=\"21\">never say this</text><text x=\"305\" y=\"533\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"21\">Formal: Cuantos anos tiene usted?</text><text x=\"305\" y=\"568\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"21\">tener again, exactly as in lesson 6</text><rect x=\"570\" y=\"105\" width=\"460\" height=\"480\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text x=\"800\" y=\"160\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"bold\">ASKING THE PRICE</text><text x=\"800\" y=\"215\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"24\">Cuanto cuesta?</text><text x=\"800\" y=\"250\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"21\">one single item</text><text x=\"800\" y=\"300\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"24\">Cuanto cuestan?</text><text x=\"800\" y=\"335\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"21\">several items</text><text x=\"800\" y=\"385\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"24\">Cuanto es?</text><text x=\"800\" y=\"420\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"21\">the total at the till</text><line x1=\"620\" y1=\"450\" x2=\"980\" y2=\"450\" stroke=\"#888\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"800\" y=\"498\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"23\">Cuesta doce euros.</text><text x=\"800\" y=\"538\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"23\">Son quince con cincuenta.</text><text x=\"800\" y=\"573\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"21\">Cuanto vale? works too in Spain</text><rect x=\"70\" y=\"620\" width=\"960\" height=\"185\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"rgba(59,130,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"670\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"bold\">READING A PRICE ALOUD</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"695\" width=\"240\" height=\"70\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"270\" y=\"740\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"26\">12,50 euros</text><path d=\"M 410 730 L 500 730\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><path d=\"M 480 713 L 504 730 L 480 747 Z\" fill=\"#ffd700\"/><text x=\"530\" y=\"740\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"24\">doce euros con cincuenta</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"792\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-size=\"22\">Spanish uses a comma where English uses a point.</text><rect x=\"70\" y=\"835\" width=\"960\" height=\"165\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"883\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-size=\"26\" font-weight=\"bold\">IN A SHOP</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"928\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Cuanto cuesta la camiseta?  -  Cuesta veinte euros.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"972\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Cuanto es todo?  -  Son treinta y cinco euros.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Age is something you have, not something you are; prices come in three question shapes depending on what you are counting."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "application",
     "title": "Say It Out Loud: Five Numbers About You",
     "content": "Numbers only become automatic when they come out of your own mouth about your own life. Here are five things to say aloud, right now, before you close this lesson. Nobody has to hear you.\n\n**1. Your phone number.** Digit by digit is always understood: **seis, uno, cuatro, dos, ocho…** In Spain people usually group the digits in pairs instead — 91 234 56 78 becomes *noventa y uno, veintitrés, cuatro, cincuenta y seis, setenta y ocho* — but nobody will blink at one digit at a time. Say: **Mi número de teléfono es…**\n\n**2. Your birthday.** **Mi cumpleaños es el…** (mee koom-pleh-AH-nyohs) — day, then **de**, then the month. **Mi cumpleaños es el cuatro de julio.** No year needed unless someone asks.\n\n**3. The time right now.** Look at a clock and say it. Check yourself on the one thing that matters: is the hour you are naming **one**? Then **Es la una…**. Anything else? **Son las…**. Add **de la mañana**, **de la tarde** or **de la noche**.\n\n**4. Your age.** **Tengo ___ años.** Not *soy*. If the number ends in one, remember it shortens: **treinta y un años**, not *treinta y uno años*.\n\n**5. The price of something in front of you.** Pick up whatever is nearest and say **Cuesta ___ euros** — or pesos, or dollars, whichever you will actually use. If there are decimals, join them with **con**.\n\nOne final drill, and it is the useful one. Say today's full date, then say the time, then say your age, as three sentences in a row without stopping:\n\n**Hoy es el seis de agosto de dos mil veintiséis. Son las nueve y media de la mañana. Tengo treinta y cuatro años.**\n\nThat is three of the most common things anyone will ever ask you, answered without hesitation. Come back to this card tomorrow and say it again with the new date and the new time — a minute a day for a week and the whole system stops being arithmetic and starts being language.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">FIVE THINGS TO SAY ALOUD</text><rect x=\"70\" y=\"100\" width=\"960\" height=\"150\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"145\" cy=\"175\" r=\"34\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"145\" y=\"187\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-size=\"30\" font-weight=\"bold\">1</text><text x=\"215\" y=\"152\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-size=\"25\" font-weight=\"bold\">YOUR PHONE NUMBER</text><text x=\"215\" y=\"196\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Mi numero de telefono es seis, uno, cuatro...</text><text x=\"215\" y=\"232\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">digit by digit is always understood</text><rect x=\"70\" y=\"275\" width=\"960\" height=\"150\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"145\" cy=\"350\" r=\"34\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"145\" y=\"362\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"30\" font-weight=\"bold\">2</text><text x=\"215\" y=\"327\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"25\" font-weight=\"bold\">YOUR BIRTHDAY</text><text x=\"215\" y=\"371\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Mi cumpleanos es el cuatro de julio.</text><text x=\"215\" y=\"407\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">day, then de, then the month</text><rect x=\"70\" y=\"450\" width=\"960\" height=\"150\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"145\" cy=\"525\" r=\"34\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"145\" y=\"537\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-size=\"30\" font-weight=\"bold\">3</text><text x=\"215\" y=\"502\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-size=\"25\" font-weight=\"bold\">THE TIME RIGHT NOW</text><text x=\"215\" y=\"546\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Son las nueve y media de la manana.</text><text x=\"215\" y=\"582\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">es for one o clock, son for every other hour</text><rect x=\"70\" y=\"625\" width=\"960\" height=\"150\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"145\" cy=\"700\" r=\"34\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"145\" y=\"712\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-size=\"30\" font-weight=\"bold\">4</text><text x=\"215\" y=\"677\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-size=\"25\" font-weight=\"bold\">YOUR AGE</text><text x=\"215\" y=\"721\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Tengo treinta y cuatro anos.</text><text x=\"215\" y=\"757\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">tener, never ser</text><rect x=\"70\" y=\"800\" width=\"960\" height=\"150\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"rgba(236,72,153,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"145\" cy=\"875\" r=\"34\" fill=\"rgba(236,72,153,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"145\" y=\"887\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-size=\"30\" font-weight=\"bold\">5</text><text x=\"215\" y=\"852\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-size=\"25\" font-weight=\"bold\">A PRICE NEAR YOU</text><text x=\"215\" y=\"896\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Cuesta cuatro euros con cincuenta.</text><text x=\"215\" y=\"932\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">join the decimals with con</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"995\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"24\" font-weight=\"bold\">One minute a day and this stops being arithmetic.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Five sentences about your own life that turn the whole numbering system into something you can produce on demand."
     }
    }
