     "type": "example",
     "title": "A Whole Meal, From the Door to the Bill",
     "content": "Read this straight through first. You will understand more of it than you expect, because almost every word has already appeared in this lesson or an earlier one.\n\n**TÚ:** Buenas noches. Una mesa para dos, por favor.\n*Good evening. A table for two, please.*\n\n**CAMARERO:** Por aquí, por favor. Aquí tienen la carta.\n*This way, please. Here is the menu.* (Literally \"here you-plural have the menu\" — a very common way to hand something over.)\n\n**TÚ:** Gracias. ¿Cuál es el menú del día?\n*Thank you. What is today's set menu?*\n\n**CAMARERO:** De primero, sopa o ensalada. De segundo, pollo asado o pescado. De postre, fruta o helado.\n*For the first course, soup or salad. For the second, roast chicken or fish. For dessert, fruit or ice cream.*\n\n**TÚ:** ¿Qué me recomienda?\n*What do you recommend?*\n\n**CAMARERO:** El pescado está muy bueno hoy.\n*The fish is very good today.*\n\n**TÚ:** Muy bien. Para mí, la ensalada y el pescado. Y para ella, el pollo, por favor.\n*Very good. For me, the salad and the fish. And for her, the chicken, please.*\n\n**CAMARERO:** ¿Y para beber?\n*And to drink?*\n\n**TÚ:** Una botella de agua y una copa de vino tinto.\n*A bottle of water and a glass of red wine.*\n\n*(later)*\n\n**CAMARERO:** ¿Todo bien?\n*Everything all right?*\n\n**TÚ:** Sí, todo está muy bueno, gracias. La cuenta, por favor. ¿Está incluida la propina?\n*Yes, everything is very good, thank you. The bill, please. Is the tip included?*\n\n**CAMARERO:** El servicio está incluido, sí.\n*The service charge is included, yes.*\n\n**WHAT TO NOTICE**\n\n• Not one sentence in there is complicated. The longest is nine words.\n• **Está muy bueno** rather than **es muy bueno** — you are describing how the food tastes tonight, not making a permanent claim about fish.\n• **Aquí tienen** and **¿Y para beber?** show how much Spanish leaves out. The waiter never says *what would you like to drink* — four words do it.\n• You could survive this entire meal with **por favor**, **gracias**, **para mí** and a finger pointed at the menu. Everything else is upgrade.",
