     "explanation": "For a friend, the affirmative command is the él/ella present form, so **hablar** gives **habla**. But **venir** is one of the eight irregulars, so it is **ven**, not **viene**. The forms with -s (**hablas**, **vienes**) are ordinary statements — \"you speak\", \"you come\" — not commands. And **hable / venga** are the polite usted commands, correct Spanish but wrong register for a friend.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">BUILDING A TU COMMAND</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"105\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"22\">Two questions, and you are done</text><circle cx=\"130\" cy=\"230\" r=\"42\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"245\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"38\">1</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"160\" width=\"840\" height=\"140\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"245\" y=\"215\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">Is it one of the eight irregulars?</text><text x=\"245\" y=\"265\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">di, haz, ve, pon, sal, se, ten, ven</text><circle cx=\"130\" cy=\"420\" r=\"42\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"435\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"38\">2</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"350\" width=\"840\" height=\"140\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"245\" y=\"405\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">If NO: use the he/she present form</text><text x=\"245\" y=\"455\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">mirar to el mira to Mira!</text><circle cx=\"130\" cy=\"610\" r=\"42\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"625\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"38\">3</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"540\" width=\"840\" height=\"140\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"245\" y=\"595\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">If YES: use the memorised word</text><text x=\"245\" y=\"645\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">There is nothing to build. Just recall it.</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"740\" width=\"980\" height=\"260\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"800\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"28\">THE CLASSIC SLIP</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"855\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"24\">Hablas mas despacio  =  You speak more slowly.</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"900\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"24\">That is a statement, not a command.</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"960\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"22\">The -s ending belongs to the you form, not the command.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Two questions build any informal command: is it irregular, and if not, what is the él form?"
     }
